'''Amblycephalus''' (am-bli-sef′a-lus), ''n.'' [NL., < Gr. ἀμβλύς, blunt, + κεφαλή, head.] '''1.''' In ''herpet.'', the bluntheads, a genus of colubriform serpents founded by Kuhl in 1827, considered by some an aberrant form of ''Dipsadidæ.'' {{smaller|''A. boa'' inhabits Java, Borneo, and neighboring islands. Also written ''Amblicephalus.''}} '''2.''' In ''entom.'', a genus of homopterous hemipterous insects, family ''Cercopidæ:'' a name preoccupied in herpetology. ''A. interruptus'', a kind of hop-frog or froth-fly, injures hops.

'''Amblychila''' (am-bli-kī′lä), ''n.'' [NL., < Gr. ἀμβλύς, blunt, obtuse, + χεῖλος, lip.] A genus of ''Cicindelidæ'', or tiger-beetles, peculiar to North America.
[[FIGURE]]
{{c|{{smaller|Tiger-beetle (''Amblychila cylindriformis''), slightly magnified.}}}}
